WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.119 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  supermarket worker Yesenia and her two  young children Jorge and Jasmine are  fleeing they say for their lives across  the sukiyaki River from Guatemala to  Mexico they tried first across the  border bridge with a caravan and  thousands of Central Americans trying to  reach the US Yesenia told us why thanks  just come to extort you and you have to  pay all there's a gun to your head they  asked me for half my salary of the $20  zone a day I'd have to give them ten and  I have to provide for my children there  wasn't enough left Mexican authorities  weren't prepared to let the caravan go  through the bridge crossing together  only in small groups the migrants feared  that would just lead to deportation so a  mass exodus began to the water  everyone's now decided that crossing the  bridge of trying to cross it isn't worth  it so they're crossing the river that's  right next to it with the helping hand  they made it  what good did it do closing the gates if  we were going to cross anyway which she  spoke too soon Mexico's security forces  were waiting chaos broke out  Yesenia dropped the rocks out with  everything they had and they scrambled  up the banks at the top a race between  the National Guard and migrants to  outflank each other many people got  through or resisted attempts to detain  them we saw the National Guard push  people back but refrain from using  excessive force but some tear gas did  get into Jorge's eyes it was too much  for him and Yesenia we're going back but  we'll try and go again we have to cross  whatever happens I need a better life  for my children but just as they were  heading back to the river and migration  agent arrived with food water  I need asylum there are too many  criminals in Guatemala Yesenia and her  family were taken to a health clinic and  then let go but many were less lucky and  hundreds ended the afternoon on the  Mexican bank of the sukiyaki River John  Holman al-jazeera Ciudad de al gore

